thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 1568, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 1568, "cached_input": 26918, "input": 28488, "output": 204}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 30781, "other": 423, "system": 35826, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 1831}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 83258}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "c4ba803c-f008-5e03-ba8b-1cec1b019c7c", "at": 1795685650.56633, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83172, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "5ead517f-dfc2-5914-8462-2f0780e01356", "at": 1795685651.71382, "until": 1795685651.7375402, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83173, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (10 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "96bf484a-3216-5751-8ea9-5e0acc0e1f5b", "at": 1795685651.739542, "until": 1795685652.4189878, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83184, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01Q9jfiogxEnwW8ob1Y5n6U9", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "forge api repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline 2>&1 | python3 -c \" import sys,json,base64 d=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode() if 'content_base64' in d else str(d) print(len(t));print(t[:6000])\"", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "forge api repos/world/story-repo/wiki/page/Outline 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json,base64\nd=json.load(sys.stdin);t=base64.b64decode(d['content_base64']).decode() if 'content_base64' in d else str(d)\nprint(len(t));print(t[:6000])\""]], "output": "```console\n29073\n# Outline (revision 6): after the idea review, the venue request, results-v1 and Brief rev 3 — story-repo\n\nWorking from: `Brief` of idea-repo (revision 3), objective `story-repo#1`. This page says **what to test and what each part of the paper says**; it never says what a result must be. Where a result decides between two stories, both are written below (§6) so nobody has to rewrite the paper's frame after the fact.\n\n## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\nNeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item is checked against the evidence.\n\n## 0. The paper in one paragraph\nEvaluating an LLM on a full benchmark is costly, so we run it on n ≪ N items and predict its full score. Existing methods (anchor points, tinyBenchmarks, metabench, assessor, active acquisition) use the score matrix of *source models* to pick items and fit a *latent model* of the target; they are judged mostly on held-out models that resemble the sources. We cast the problem as **finite-population estimation of a mean of N unknown 0/1 values with a free covariate (the source matrix)**. That frame separates what the sources can buy — **variance reduction** — from what must be controlled by design — **bias**. We (i) test, on 13 binary matrices and under three target splits (interpolation, extrapolation, lineage-held-out), whether model-based predictors lose accuracy where targets differ from the sources; (ii) test whether a design-based correction (probability sampling with a positivity floor + difference/GREG estimator) repairs it and at what variance cost; (iii) measure how much the source matrix can help at all over plain stratified/balanced random sampling; (iv) examine ordering of models separately from score error. A negative or conditional answer to any of these is a result.\n\nWorking title (not final): *What do source models buy? Design-based benchmark prediction from a few items.*\n\n## 1. Claims, evidence each needs, and the figure/table that carries it\nPrimary endpoint (fixed before running): **RMSE ratio to uniform random sampling at n = 100 items, geometric mean over benchmarks, paired clustered bootstrap CI, per split.** One **secondary** endpoint at fixed n/N = 2% (n = 100 is ~18% of IFEval, N≈541, but <1% of MMLU-Pro, N≈12k, so the geometric mean mixes very different n/N). Conclusions must hold at both n=100 and n/N=2%, or are reported as scale-dependent. Neither is changed after seeing curves. Everything else is secondary.\n\n| # | Claim (to be tested) | Evidence needed from analysis | Carried by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C0 | Setting and protocol are sound: item selection/tuning use sources only, same n for all methods, shared seeds, one subset serves all targets in a draw | Data audit (per file: N, #models, score range, binary-ness, families); leakage checks; `benchpred` cross-check | Table 1 (audit, main or appendix by venue budget); protocol Fig. 1 |\n| C1 | **Comparison:** how do model-based, anchor-based and design-based methods rank by the pr\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "86450dc4-2e63-5a29-a2b8-da3831b6f7a3", "at": 1795685652.231634, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83186, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "ed8529f9-6bd5-581a-ae95-d465872df69d", "at": 1795685652.2334342, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83187, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "d8383c9f-4310-56ca-b875-7639f23cbe76", "at": 1795685652.2461686, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 83188, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "679869f419134d62d1c7fad35f521fad", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguo